20:T631,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What does each part of an IFSC code mean?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The first four letters identify the bank, the fifth character is zero, and the last six characters identify the branch."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the IFSC the same as the MICR code?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The IFSC is an 11-character alphanumeric code used for electronic transfers. MICR is a 9-digit code printed on cheques that is used for cheque clearing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if my transfer fails because of a wrong IFSC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The money is normally returned to your account within a few working days. Contact your bank if the refund does not arrive, and re-enter the correct IFSC for the next attempt."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do all branches of a bank share one IFSC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Every branch has its own IFSC, so use the code of the branch where the account is held."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the IFSC Finder free on ContentVerse India?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. All India utility tools on ContentVerse India are free to use with no sign-up required."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this an official government website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. ContentVerse India is an independent platform. We use public datasets and open APIs. For official records, use government portals like Parivahan, GST, FoSCoS, or ECI."}}]}21:T851,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to use IFSC Finder","description":"IFSC (Indian Financial System Code) is an 11-character code that identifies a specific bank branch for electronic transfers such as NEFT, RTGS and IMPS. A wrong IFSC can delay a payment or send it back, so it is worth checking before you add a beneficiary. This free IFSC finder shows the bank name, ","url":"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/ifsc-finder","totalTime":"PT5M","tool":{"@type":"HowToTool","name":"IFSC Finder"},"step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"How to find an IFSC code step by step","text":"Type the 11-character IFSC into the box and press “Find branch”. The tool shows the bank, branch, district and state it belongs to. Check that they match your passbook, cheque book or the beneficiary’s details. If you do not have the code, find it on a cheque leaf, in your net-banking profile or on the bank’s official branch locator, then paste it here to verify."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"How an IFSC code is structured","text":"The first four characters are letters that identify the bank, for example SBIN for State Bank of India or HDFC for HDFC Bank. The fifth character is always the digit zero, reserved for future use. The last six characters are letters or digits identifying the branch."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"NEFT, RTGS and IMPS: when the IFSC is needed","text":"NEFT, RTGS and IMPS to a new beneficiary all use the account number together with the IFSC. UPI usually uses a VPA or a mobile number instead, but UPI payments linked to a bank account still use the IFSC behind the scenes. Salary credits, EMI mandates, mutual fund redemptions and tax refunds also rely on a correct IFSC."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Common IFSC mistakes and how to avoid them","text":"Branches merge and banks amalgamate. After a merger, branches may get a new IFSC and the old one may stop working. If a transfer fails, check whether your bank has recently merged with another. Using the latest code from your bank’s website or passbook avoids this."}]}16:[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"IFSC Finder\",\"alternateName\":\"IFSC Code Finder — Bank Branch Details India\",\"description\":\"Find bank name, branch address, MICR, and payment modes (NEFT, RTGS, IMPS, UPI) from any Indian IFSC code. Free lookup.\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/ifsc-finder\",\"applicationCategory\":\"UtilitiesApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Any\",\"browserRequirements\":\"Requires JavaScript\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"0\",\"priceCurrency\":\"INR\"},\"provider\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"ContentVerse India\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-IN\",\"featureList\":\"How to find an IFSC code step by step, How an IFSC code is structured, NEFT, RTGS and IMPS: when the IFSC is needed, Common IFSC mistakes and how to avoid them\"}"}}],["$","script","1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$20"}}],["$","script","2",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"India Tools\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"IFSC Finder\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/ifsc-finder\"}]}"}}],["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$21"}}]],"$L22"]
