"How to use ","IFSC Finder"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"IFSC (Indian Financial System Code) is an 11-character code that identifies a specific bank branch for electronic transfers such as NEFT, RTGS and IMPS. A wrong IFSC can delay a payment or send it back, so it is worth checking before you add a beneficiary. This free IFSC finder shows the bank name, branch, address, MICR code and supported payment modes for any IFSC, and helps you find a code when you only know the bank and city."}]]}],["$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29"]]}],"$L2a","$L2b","$L2c","$L2d","$L2e"]}],"$L2f"]}],"$L30"]}]
