27:["$","div","How an IFSC code is structured",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"How an IFSC code is structured"}],[["$","p","The first four characters are letters that ident",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"The first four characters are letters that identify the bank, for example SBIN for State Bank of India or HDFC for HDFC Bank. The fifth character is always the digit zero, reserved for future use. The last six characters are letters or digits identifying the branch."}],["$","p","Because the format is fixed, many errors can be ",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Because the format is fixed, many errors can be spotted at a glance: a code that is shorter than 11 characters, has a letter instead of the zero in the fifth position, or has an unknown bank prefix is probably mistyped."}]],null,null]}]
28:["$","div","NEFT, RTGS and IMPS: when the IFSC is needed",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"NEFT, RTGS and IMPS: when the IFSC is needed"}],[["$","p","NEFT, RTGS and IMPS to a new beneficiary all use",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"NEFT, RTGS and IMPS to a new beneficiary all use the account number together with the IFSC. UPI usually uses a VPA or a mobile number instead, but UPI payments linked to a bank account still use the IFSC behind the scenes. Salary credits, EMI mandates, mutual fund redemptions and tax refunds also rely on a correct IFSC."}],["$","p","The result also shows which payment modes the br",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"The result also shows which payment modes the branch supports where that data is available, so you can pick the right mode for large or urgent payments."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","li","NEFT: any amount, settles in batches throughout the day",{"children":"NEFT: any amount, settles in batches throughout the day"}],["$","li","RTGS: usually for high-value transfers above ₹2 lakh, settles in real time",{"children":"RTGS: usually for high-value transfers above ₹2 lakh, settles in real time"}],["$","li","IMPS: instant, available round the clock",{"children":"IMPS: instant, available round the clock"}]]}],null]}]
29:["$","div","Common IFSC mistakes and how to avoid them",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"Common IFSC mistakes and how to avoid them"}],[["$","p","Branches merge and banks amalgamate. After a mer",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Branches merge and banks amalgamate. After a merger, branches may get a new IFSC and the old one may stop working. If a transfer fails, check whether your bank has recently merged with another. Using the latest code from your bank’s website or passbook avoids this."}],["$","p","Never rely on an IFSC received only over an unve",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Never rely on an IFSC received only over an unverified message. Fraudsters sometimes send altered bank details. Confirm the beneficiary’s name and account number as well as the code before you confirm a payment."}]],null,null]}]
